# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# The repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf converts on checkout) but
# Tools/Coverage/report.sh and the RebuildScripts.sh template are executed on
# Linux/macOS. A CRLF shebang fails as:
#     bash: /usr/bin/env bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
# which is a confusing way to find out about line endings.
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.sh.in  text eol=lf
*.bash   text eol=lf

# CMake and source files keep the platform default; the tree is predominantly
# CRLF today and normalising it would be a whole-repo diff for no benefit.
